Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.70,0:00:40.39,Main,Nelson,0,0,0,,Hey, Van'er.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.88,0:00:46.45,Main,Van'er,0,0,0,,Why are you guys here?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.45,0:00:47.62,Main,Rodney,0,0,0,,Aren't you here too?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.62,0:00:49.99,Main,Nelson,0,0,0,,Ten silver royals a month, plus meals.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.99,0:00:51.33,Main,Nelson,0,0,0,,You'd be a fool not to come.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.33,0:00:54.72,Main,Nelson,0,0,0,,Besides, we're just here to \Ndo odd jobs for the knights.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.72,0:00:56.56,Main,Nelson,0,0,0,,We're not actually going into battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.56,0:00:58.16,Main,Nelson,0,0,0,,If things look bad, I'll run.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.16,0:00:59.55,Main,Nelson,0,0,0,,If I can outrun you, I'm good.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.55,0:01:01.82,Main,Rodney,0,0,0,,Speaking of which, if you kick the bucket,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.82,0:01:03.86,Main,Rodney,0,0,0,,what will happen to the girl you're \Nseeing at the tavern in town?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.86,0:01:05.93,Main,Nelson,0,0,0,,Oh yeah, that Shirley girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.76,0:01:09.56,Main,Van'er,0,0,0,,Nonsense. I'm not going to die here.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.56,0:01:11.37,Main,Van'er,0,0,0,,I'm going to propose next year.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.37,0:01:13.10,Main,Van'er,0,0,0,,I'm just here to make some money.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.10,0:01:14.43,Main,Van'er,0,0,0,,How else am I supposed to marry her?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.36,0:01:17.60,Main,Nelson,0,0,0,,If you die, the death \Nbenefits will be even more.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.60,0:01:19.92,Main,Van'er,0,0,0,,Pah, I'm not that stupid.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.92,0:01:21.12,Main,Van'er,0,0,0,,Wouldn't that just benefit someone else?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.12,0:01:22.24,Main,Rodney,0,0,0,,Don't be silly.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.24,0:01:23.67,Main,Rodney,0,0,0,,Getting paid is good enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.67,0:01:25.15,Main,Rodney,0,0,0,,A death benefit?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.15,0:01:27.16,Main,Rodney,0,0,0,,Thirty silver royals won't \Nbe enough to marry her.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.16,0:01:28.43,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Quiet!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.98,0:01:31.47,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Everyone, stand at attention \Nand form a line.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.47,0:01:33.48,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,His Highness Roland Wimbledon,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.48,0:01:35.61,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Fourth Prince of the Kingdom \Nof Graycastle, has arrived.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.19,0:03:47.39,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,First of all, I want to thank you \Nall for bravely stepping forward
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.39,0:03:49.72,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,to contribute to the \Ndefense of our homeland.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.32,0:03:54.39,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,From now on, you are members \Nof the Border Town militia.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.39,0:03:56.42,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Over the next month and a half,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.42,0:03:58.74,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,you will undergo rigorous training.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.74,0:03:59.76,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Of course,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.76,0:04:02.30,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,rigorous training will come with rewards.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.30,0:04:04.08,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,If you pass the training,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.08,0:04:05.69,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,you will receive a reward.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.69,0:04:07.06,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,That reward is
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.06,0:04:09.55,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,an extra egg in everyone's lunch today.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.59,0:04:16.39,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Now, let me introduce your captain.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.56,0:04:28.67,Main,Militia,0,0,0,,Isn't that Iron Axe?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.67,0:04:30.67,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I'm sure you all know him.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.67,0:04:32.31,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Iron Axe is our finest hunter,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.31,0:04:34.44,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,and he's willing to fight \Nto defend Border Town.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.44,0:04:36.46,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I thank him for this.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.46,0:04:39.36,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I also promise you all, \Nin the name of Roland Wimbledon,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.36,0:04:43.26,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,that anyone who excels in training \Nor fights bravely on the battlefield
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.26,0:04:46.06,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,will be granted an official rank, \Nregardless of their background.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.67,0:04:49.00,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,All right, Iron Axe, begin the training.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.00,0:04:50.48,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.22,0:04:53.52,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,Attention, everyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.52,0:04:56.18,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,We will now begin the \Nfirst training exercise.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.90,0:04:59.29,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,Stand at attention.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.29,0:05:02.79,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,Everyone, adopt my posture and \Nremain standing for half an hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.79,0:05:05.36,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,As long as you can stay completely \Nstill for half an hour,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.36,0:05:08.43,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,everyone will get an extra egg for lunch.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.82,0:05:13.37,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,Chest out, head up,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.93,0:05:16.19,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,buttocks up, stomach in.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.93,0:05:21.38,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,Arms straight down by your sides.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.50,0:05:24.19,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,Do not move a muscle.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.19,0:05:25.54,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,Maintain this for half an hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.54,0:05:27.16,Main,Van'er,0,0,0,,Hang in there, Van'er.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.93,0:05:29.34,Main,Van'er,0,0,0,,Just hold on a little longer,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.04,0:05:31.93,Main,Van'er,0,0,0,,and you'll get that egg.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.42,0:05:39.93,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,Time's up.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.71,0:05:52.26,Main,Nelson,0,0,0,,We did it!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.16,0:05:56.90,Main,Rodney,0,0,0,,We're getting an egg for lunch!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.75,0:05:59.51,Main,Rodney,0,0,0,,I haven't had one in a year.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.60,0:06:02.79,Main,Nelson,0,0,0,,Van'er, are you okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.79,0:06:03.82,Main,Van'er,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.62,0:06:06.60,Main,Van'er,0,0,0,,I never thought just standing still
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.60,0:06:08.64,Main,Van'er,0,0,0,,would be more tiring \Nthan being a stonemason.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.43,0:06:21.13,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,The first round of training is complete.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.13,0:06:23.64,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,Everyone has finished the exercise.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.07,0:06:28.83,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Carter.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.57,0:06:30.64,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.02,0:06:40.07,Main,Rodney,0,0,0,,What's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.07,0:06:43.07,Main,Rodney,0,0,0,,They're not going back on their word \Nand taking away the egg, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.07,0:06:44.40,Main,Van'er,0,0,0,,What are you thinking?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.40,0:06:46.88,Main,Van'er,0,0,0,,The Prince promised, \Nso why would he go back on it?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.88,0:06:49.79,Main,Nelson,0,0,0,,Hey, when it comes to what the nobles say,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.79,0:06:51.55,Main,Nelson,0,0,0,,it's about as reliable as a fart.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.55,0:06:54.24,Main,Van'er,0,0,0,,The Prince wouldn't go \Nback on his word, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.24,0:06:56.88,Main,Rodney,0,0,0,,Come to think of it, \Nthis Prince is pretty strange.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.88,0:06:58.71,Main,Rodney,0,0,0,,He actually made Iron Axe the captain.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.71,0:07:00.39,Main,Rodney,0,0,0,,Iron Axe is a Sand person.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.39,0:07:02.52,Main,Rodney,0,0,0,,Aren't nobles all about bloodlines?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.52,0:07:04.35,Main,Van'er,0,0,0,,Iron Axe is a decent guy.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.35,0:07:06.64,Main,Nelson,0,0,0,,He's the most skilled hunter in town.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.64,0:07:09.90,Main,Nelson,0,0,0,,Ah, sometimes I really \Nenvy the Sand people.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.90,0:07:13.02,Main,Nelson,0,0,0,,With a physique like that, \Nyou could stand forever without trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.52,0:07:17.51,Main,Van'er,0,0,0,,Hey, be quiet.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.51,0:07:20.02,Main,Van'er,0,0,0,,Look, the knight is back.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.19,0:07:33.89,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,A message from His Highness \NRoland Wimbledon:
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.22,0:07:36.89,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,"Everyone did well. Good work.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.37,0:07:40.27,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,For today's lunch, \Neveryone gets an extra egg."
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.12,0:07:46.02,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Quiet. His Highness has \Nfurther instructions.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.02,0:07:47.68,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,The second round of \Ntraining will now begin.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.68,0:07:49.39,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Continue standing at \Nattention for one hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.85,0:07:51.88,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,If, once again, no one moves,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.88,0:07:53.89,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,everyone gets another egg for lunch.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.89,0:07:56.85,Main,Rodney,0,0,0,,Two eggs? My goodness...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.33,0:08:03.55,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,However, if even a single \Nperson fails to hold out,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.55,0:08:05.70,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,the training will be considered a failure,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.70,0:08:08.35,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,and no one will get the second egg.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.35,0:08:10.34,Main,Nelson,0,0,0,,Wh-What is the meaning of this?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.34,0:08:12.54,Main,Nelson,0,0,0,,Some kind of noble prank?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.54,0:08:14.78,Main,Rodney,0,0,0,,But if just one person \Nfails to hold out...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.78,0:08:16.85,Main,Rodney,0,0,0,,How am I supposed to know \Nif the others can hold out?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.28,0:08:18.57,Main,Rodney,0,0,0,,What about you, Van'er?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.57,0:08:20.07,Main,Rodney,0,0,0,,Can you do it one more time?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.73,0:08:25.70,Main,Van'er,0,0,0,,For that second egg, I'm going all out!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.14,0:08:38.27,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,It looks like you have something \Nto say to me, Carter.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.31,0:08:42.35,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,It's all right, go ahead.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.95,0:08:47.10,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Your Highness, I would \Nnever question your decision.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.67,0:08:51.32,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,However, these men are nothing \Nbut a ragtag mob.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.72,0:08:54.17,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,I've seen it too many times.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.17,0:08:56.50,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Once they're on the battlefield, \Nthey're the first to run.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.50,0:08:58.37,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,And to be honest,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.37,0:09:01.04,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,I don't see the point \Nof this training either.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.04,0:09:04.00,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,We can't defeat the demonic beasts \Njust by standing still, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.00,0:09:06.54,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Right now, the nobles and \Nknights aren't on our side.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.54,0:09:10.28,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,I was ready to risk my life to at least \Nteach these men how to wield a sword.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.28,0:09:13.99,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,And besides, are you really going to \Nmake that Sand person the captain?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.99,0:09:16.99,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,He doesn't belong to Graycastle, \Nnor to any kingdom on the continent.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.49,0:09:21.15,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Using your methods,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.15,0:09:22.44,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,could you train them into warriors
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.44,0:09:24.30,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,capable of fighting \Nthe beasts within two months?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.30,0:09:26.22,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,That's... impossible.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.07,0:09:29.59,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,In my experience, \Nit takes at least five years.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.59,0:09:31.85,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,And another five {years }to reach \Nthe standard of a knight.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.85,0:09:35.87,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,That's precisely why I'm not training \Nthem to be warriors or knights.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.87,0:09:38.50,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I know exactly what I can \Nachieve in just two months.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.50,0:09:40.51,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,You'll soon see the \Nresults of this training.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.51,0:09:41.85,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.85,0:09:44.58,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,As for Iron Axe, witches don't \Nbelong to Graycastle either,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.58,0:09:46.19,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,yet they all belong to Border Town.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.19,0:09:49.01,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Besides, aren't you here \Nto keep an eye on things?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.01,0:09:52.05,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Instead of worrying about a \NSand person, you should focus on this.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.05,0:09:52.85,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.38,0:09:55.00,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,This is the schedule for the coming days.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.00,0:09:57.58,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,All future training must \Nstrictly adhere to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.58,0:09:58.28,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.89,0:10:05.23,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,But, Your Highness...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.23,0:10:08.01,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,I understand the running \Ndrills and roll calls,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.01,0:10:09.46,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,but this last point...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.46,0:10:12.50,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Are you really going to have \Nthem learn to read and write?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.50,0:10:15.04,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Just enough so they can read and \Nwrite orders as quickly as possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.04,0:10:17.35,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I'll explain this part to Karl myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.94,0:10:21.35,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,But that's of no use in battle!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.35,0:10:22.15,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Who said that?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.76,0:10:26.15,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,A unit skilled in combat is \Ninevitably a cultured unit.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.42,0:10:29.35,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,This is a lesson learned from history.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.68,0:10:40.58,Main,Guards,0,0,0,,Line up to get your lunch. No pushing.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.58,0:10:43.10,Main,Guards,0,0,0,,Maintain order. Everyone gets a share.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.53,0:11:12.56,Main,Nelson,0,0,0,,If we get a meal like this every day,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.56,0:11:14.72,Main,Nelson,0,0,0,,standing a few more \Nhours would be worth it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.10,0:11:16.52,Main,Rodney,0,0,0,,At least it's just standing.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.52,0:11:19.60,Main,Rodney,0,0,0,,I wonder what other tricks \Nthis Prince has up his sleeve.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.65,0:11:23.82,Main,Van'er,0,0,0,,Who cares?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.82,0:11:26.16,Main,Van'er,0,0,0,,As long as there's food, I'll do anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.35,0:11:49.88,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,The afternoon training begins at the \NHour of the Deer and ends at sunset.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.88,0:11:52.47,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Everyone will jog three \Nlaps around Border Town.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.47,0:11:53.90,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Everyone must complete it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.90,0:11:56.68,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,Understood. What if someone falls behind?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.97,0:11:58.74,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,They can help each other.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.74,0:12:00.68,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,Support, pull, carry...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.68,0:12:03.85,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,No matter what it takes,\Neveryone must finish.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.85,0:12:05.68,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,That is the Prince's order.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.41,0:12:10.00,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,If everyone completes the training,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.00,0:12:12.06,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,then everyone gets an \Nextra egg for dinner.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.99,0:12:14.06,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,Sounds good.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.15,0:12:17.24,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Good luck to you all.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.35,0:12:22.56,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Oh, by the way...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.18,0:12:26.64,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,After dinner, I suggest \Nyou go to bed early.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.64,0:12:28.35,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Sleep as much as you can.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.71,0:12:32.35,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,They'll sleep like logs tonight.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.01,0:12:35.29,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Is that so?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.29,0:12:37.88,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,I suggest you don't sleep too soundly.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.88,0:12:39.47,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,The afternoon training is as follows.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.47,0:12:42.11,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,From the Hour of the Deer until sunset,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.11,0:12:44.32,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,jog three laps around Border Town.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.32,0:12:48.17,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,You may help each other: \Nsupport, pull, carry.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.17,0:12:49.73,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,If you really can't keep running,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.73,0:12:51.12,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,you may rest for a moment,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.12,0:12:53.55,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,but you must persist and \Nfinish all three laps.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.55,0:12:56.81,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,If everyone completes the \Ntraining before sunset,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.81,0:12:59.31,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,an extra egg will be added to dinner.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.31,0:13:01.93,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,If even one person fails \Nto finish on time,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.93,0:13:05.44,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,then no one gets the third egg.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.73,0:13:24.18,Italics,Van'er,0,0,0,,The egg that I finally \Nmanaged to get at lunch...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.73,0:13:29.75,Italics,Van'er,0,0,0,,Have all the others already run past?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.32,0:13:31.66,Italics,Van'er,0,0,0,,Damn it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.12,0:13:35.39,Italics,Van'er,0,0,0,,I want that third egg so badly.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.39,0:13:36.57,Italics,Van'er,0,0,0,,Damn it...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.24,0:13:40.41,Italics,Van'er,0,0,0,,Get up, Van'er.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.45,0:13:39.52,Main,Nelson,0,0,0,,Van'er!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.86,0:13:42.10,Main,Nelson,0,0,0,,Van'er!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.18,0:13:43.28,Main,Rodney,0,0,0,,Van'er!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.62,0:13:45.31,Main,Passerby,0,0,0,,Van'er!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.46,0:14:03.14,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,So, did everyone finish?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.04,0:14:09.82,Main,Guards,0,0,0,,Reporting!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.08,0:14:13.64,Main,Guards,0,0,0,,We've counted. Still three missing!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.04,0:14:18.68,Main,Passerby,0,0,0,,Look! They're coming back!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.68,0:14:21.64,Main,Passerby,0,0,0,,They're back, they're back!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.49,0:14:55.39,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,Sir, everyone has reached the finish line.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.39,0:14:57.89,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,Everyone has reached the finish line!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.88,0:15:05.11,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,I can confirm that everyone \Nhas completed the training!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.99,0:15:30.97,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Today's training went well.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.02,0:15:39.47,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,There's one more session tonight.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.87,0:15:41.31,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,One more session?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.31,0:15:43.42,Main,Crowd,0,0,0,,I'm going to get a good \Nnight's sleep tonight.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.42,0:15:46.22,Main,Crowd,0,0,0,,I feel like I could fall \Nasleep the moment I lie down.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.22,0:15:47.44,Main,Crowd,0,0,0,,Me too.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.44,0:15:49.25,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,What's the evening training about?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.29,0:15:51.77,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Emergency assembly.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.54,0:16:06.23,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Good evening, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.77,0:16:11.34,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,You're working so hard.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.34,0:16:13.71,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,You just got back and still have to work.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.33,0:16:18.39,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,I ate your bacon while it was still hot.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.86,0:16:26.39,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Didn't anyone teach you to mind \Nyour manners in front of a prince?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.61,0:16:29.64,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I recall you being quite polite at first.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.85,0:16:35.64,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.77,0:16:40.77,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,But you clearly ordered dinner for two.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.77,0:16:42.52,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Wasn't that meant for me?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.35,0:17:01.18,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,I heard all the militia's expenses are \Ncoming out of your own pocket.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.73,0:17:03.52,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,As long as it protects Border Town,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.52,0:17:05.79,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,every expense is worth it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.79,0:17:08.61,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Then why are you teaching \Nthem to read and write?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.77,0:17:12.70,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Education helps them understand \Nwhat they're fighting for.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.70,0:17:14.50,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,It may not show yet,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.50,0:17:16.46,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,but it will be important \Nfor the battles ahead.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.46,0:17:18.31,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,What they're fighting for?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.31,0:17:20.22,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Aren't they fighting \Nto fill their stomachs?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.92,0:17:22.16,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,For now, yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.16,0:17:25.87,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,But I have to teach them \Nwhat fighting truly means.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.88,0:17:27.75,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,What about you?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.54,0:17:30.64,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,What does the Witch Cooperation \NAssociation fight for?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.93,0:17:35.25,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,We're just a bunch of poor souls \Ngathered together to survive.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.25,0:17:37.41,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,We don't have time to \Nthink about such things.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.56,0:17:41.08,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Just staying alive is already exhausting.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.48,0:18:32.48,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Your Highness, is this the \Nnew weapon you mentioned?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.48,0:18:36.04,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Yes. It's a weapon that can \Nkill enemies from a distance.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.04,0:18:38.47,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,It's called a musket. \NThe blacksmith just finished it yesterday.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.77,0:18:40.34,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,A ranged weapon?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.34,0:18:41.82,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Like a crossbow?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.82,0:18:44.16,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,It fires slower than a crossbow or a bow,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.16,0:18:45.92,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,but it has superior range and power.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.92,0:18:47.43,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Let me show you how to use it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.51,0:18:52.01,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Your Highness, \Nisn't this just Snow Powder?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.01,0:18:53.89,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Yes, but not exactly.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.89,0:18:56.00,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I adjusted its composition using the ice.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.00,0:18:57.52,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,You could call it enhanced Snow Powder.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.19,0:19:02.02,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I've named it "gunpowder."
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.81,0:19:06.77,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Now, do as I say.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.77,0:19:08.56,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Open the paper packet with your teeth.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.56,0:19:10.23,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Pour a little powder into the tray.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.23,0:19:11.27,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Close the lid.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.94,0:19:17.43,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Load the rest along with \Nthe bullet into the barrel.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.43,0:19:18.61,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Ram it down with the ramrod.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.79,0:19:25.53,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Raise the gun and aim at our target.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.53,0:19:27.15,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Rest the stock against your shoulder.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.20,0:19:34.50,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,All right, don't pull \Nthe trigger just yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.50,0:19:36.68,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,See the front sight on the barrel?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.68,0:19:39.39,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Stand up straight and slowly \Nplace your finger on the trigger.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.39,0:19:42.35,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Remember, the recoil is strong \Nwhen you fire, so stand firmly.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.01,0:19:43.98,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Aim.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.82,0:19:47.85,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Fire!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.19,0:20:13.09,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,This power is astonishing.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.03,0:20:16.68,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,If I had a weapon like this back then,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.99,0:20:19.68,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,my companions...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.97,0:20:25.18,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Your Highness, what's the \Nproduction volume of this thing?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.73,0:20:27.49,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Currently, we only have these two.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.49,0:20:29.54,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I've already ordered the blacksmith \Nto ramp up production.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.54,0:20:32.68,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,We should be able to produce two \Nmore before the Months of Demons.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.26,0:20:34.13,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.32,0:20:39.52,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I know what you're thinking.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.10,0:20:43.52,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,This is a powerful weapon,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.52,0:20:45.70,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,powerful enough to change \Nthe course of reality.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.00,0:20:51.52,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Yet, no matter how powerful, \Na weapon is ultimately just a tool.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.00,0:20:56.26,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,For you, the most powerful weapon \Nwill always be trust and loyalty.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.26,0:20:59.55,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Only a powerful warrior can \Nwield a powerful weapon.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.55,0:21:02.67,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,These are given to you to use, \Nnot to replace you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.22,0:21:05.85,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Carter, Iron Axe,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.29,0:21:07.87,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,use them to defend Border Town.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.90,0:21:10.36,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Defend our people.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.63,0:21:18.73,Main,Carter/Iron Axe,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.64,0:21:37.70,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,That was brilliant, my lord.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.68,0:21:50.35,Main,Ryan,0,0,0,,I heard that kid paid you a visit.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.35,0:21:53.33,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,Yes, my lord. He wanted to \Nrecruit us to fight for him.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.33,0:21:55.62,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,A pipe dream.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:00.68,0:22:02.71,Main,Ryan,0,0,0,,What's he been up to since then?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.71,0:22:05.06,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,My lord, I've had people \Ninvestigate thoroughly.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.06,0:22:07.34,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,The city wall is almost finished.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.34,0:22:10.70,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,I hear they're using some kind of \Nalchemical powder from Graycastle,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.70,0:22:13.20,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,which has sped up construction enormously.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:13.20,0:22:16.58,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,Besides that, he's recruited \Na bunch of militia.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:16.58,0:22:19.06,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,They have neither weapons nor knights,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:19.06,0:22:21.02,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,and are just messing around every day.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:21.02,0:22:22.82,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,And he's feeding them eggs!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:22.82,0:22:24.86,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,It's hilarious.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:26.17,0:22:28.06,Main,Ryan,0,0,0,,They have eggs to eat?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:28.06,0:22:29.85,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,Uh... yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.85,0:22:32.77,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,That kid bought winter \Nprovisions from Willow Town,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:32.77,0:22:34.52,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,and stored them all in his castle.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:34.52,0:22:37.83,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,My lord, that kid really \Ndoesn't know his place.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:37.83,0:22:39.57,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,In my opinion, when winter comes,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:39.57,0:22:42.06,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,he'll be crying and begging for your help.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:42.60,0:22:45.37,Main,Ryan,0,0,0,,So you're saying he now has a city wall,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:45.37,0:22:48.06,Main,Ryan,0,0,0,,an army, and provisions?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:48.57,0:22:50.11,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,Uh... well...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:50.64,0:22:51.56,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,Yes, my lord.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:51.83,0:22:52.94,Main,Ryan,0,0,0,,Boris.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:54.08,0:22:56.12,Main,Ryan,0,0,0,,Perhaps it is just as you say:
Dialogue: 0,0:22:56.12,0:22:58.28,Main,Ryan,0,0,0,,his wall is fragile,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:58.28,0:23:00.66,Main,Ryan,0,0,0,,his army is worthless,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:00.66,0:23:02.73,Main,Ryan,0,0,0,,and his supplies are limited.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:04.01,0:23:09.38,Main,Ryan,0,0,0,,However, I will not give him \Neven the slightest opportunity.
